@@ -0,0 +1,411 @@
+# FreqUI i18n Guide (zh-CN / en)
+
+This branch (`zh-cn`, based on upstream tag `3.2.1`) adds vue-i18n to FreqUI. Upstream has no
+i18n, so everything here is a patch we re-apply on upgrades. Keep changes minimal and mechanical:
+replace English literals with `t()` calls, do not refactor unrelated code.
+
+Terminology: **always** follow [I18N_GLOSSARY.md](./I18N_GLOSSARY.md).
+
+## 1. Architecture
+
+| File | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `src/i18n/index.ts` | Creates the vue-i18n instance (composition API, `legacy: false`), loads all locale files, exports helpers (`t`, `te`, `setLocale`, `getLocale`, `LOCALE_OPTIONS`, `getHumanizeDurationOptions`, `getDateFnsLocale`, `getEChartsLocale`). |
+| `src/locales/en/<group>.json` | English messages of one group (source of truth, keep the original upstream wording). |
+| `src/locales/zh-CN/<group>.json` | Chinese messages of the same group, identical key structure. |
+| `src/stores/settings.ts` | `settingsStore.locale` - persisted (localStorage key `ftUISettings`) user choice, default `zh-CN`. |
+| `src/App.vue` | Applies `settingsStore.locale` to vue-i18n, sets the Nuxt UI locale (`<UApp :locale>`) and the ECharts locale for all charts (vue-echarts `INIT_OPTIONS_KEY`). |
+| `src/pages/settings.vue` | Language switcher (中文 / English) - reference example for page translation. |
+| `src/components/layout/*` | Reference example for component translation (NavBar, NavFooter). |
+| `tests/setup.ts` | Installs i18n for component tests, pins tests to `en`. |
+| `tests/unit/i18n.spec.ts` | Checks: same group files and keys in all locales, same `{placeholders}`, no empty messages, no unescaped special characters, every literal key used in `src/` exists. |
+
+Locale files are discovered with `import.meta.glob('../locales/*/*.json', { eager: true })`.
+**Each file is mounted under its file name**: `src/locales/en/layout.json` → keys `layout.*`.
+Adding a group = adding the two JSON files; `src/i18n/index.ts` never needs editing.
+
+Default locale is `zh-CN`, fallback is `en` (a key missing in zh-CN shows English, never a raw key).
+
+Already localized globally (no work needed in components):
+
+- Nuxt UI built-in texts (table "No data", select/search placeholders, calendar, close buttons ...).
+- ECharts built-in texts (toolbox, dataZoom, time-axis month/week names).
+- `humanize-duration` output from `humanizeDurationFromSeconds()` (`1天 2小时 3分钟`) and the
+  candle chart measure tool.
+- date-fns: all patterns used by `src/utils/formatters/timeformat.ts` are numeric
+  (`yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss`), so no locale is needed. If you add a pattern with month/day names
+  (`MMM`, `EEE`, `PPP` ...), pass `{ locale: getDateFnsLocale() }`.
+
+## 2. Group ownership - one JSON per group
+
+| Group / namespace | Owner | Files |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `common` | infra (do not edit) | shared vocabulary: `common.actions.*`, `common.status.*`, `common.terms.*`, `common.time.*` |
+| `layout` | infra (done) | `src/App.vue`, `src/components/layout/*` |
+| `settings` | infra (done) | `src/pages/settings.vue` |
+| `ftbotA` | translator A | `src/components/ftbot/` Backtest*, Bot*, CustomTrade*, DownloadDataMain, BackgroundJobTracking |
+| `ftbotB` | translator B | `src/components/ftbot/` ExchangeSelect … TradeProfit (trading, pairs, locks, trade details) |
+| `chartsPages` | translator C | `src/components/charts/*`, `src/pages/*` (except settings), `src/components/ftbot/{Lookahead,Recursive}Analysis*` |
+| `general` | translator D | `src/components/general/*`, `src/components/*.vue`, `src/components/ftbot/PairlistConfig*`, user-visible strings in `src/stores`, `src/composables`, `src/utils` |
+
+The exact file lists are in the [appendix](#appendix-file-assignment).
+
+Rules:
+
+1. A translator writes **only** `src/locales/en/<group>.json` and `src/locales/zh-CN/<group>.json`
+   of their own group, plus the source files assigned to them. Never edit another group's JSON
+   (including `common.json`) - parallel work must not touch the same file.
+2. You may **use** keys from `common.*` (read-only). If the shared term you need does not exist,
+   add it to your own group file instead.
+3. Every key must exist in both locales (the unit test fails otherwise). The English text is the
+   original upstream text (keep it verbatim, including its capitalization).
+
+## 3. Key naming
+
+```
+<group>.<component>.<key>
+<group>.<component>.<section>.<key>
+```
+
+- `<group>`: the JSON file name (`ftbotA`, `ftbotB`, `chartsPages`, `general`, ...).
+- `<component>`: camelCase name of the source file without extension:
+  `TradeList.vue` → `tradeList`, `BacktestRun.vue` → `backtestRun`.
+  Pages get a `Page` suffix: `pages/backtest.vue` → `backtestPage`, `pages/[...path].vue` → `notFoundPage`.
+  TS modules: `stores/ftbot.ts` → `ftbotStore`, `utils/backtestMetrics.ts` → `backtestMetrics`,
+  `composables/pairTemplates.ts` → `pairTemplates`.
+- `<key>` / `<section>`: camelCase English, describing the meaning (not a copy of the text).
+  Useful sections: `columns`, `actions`, `fields`, `hints`, `alerts`, `options`, `tooltips`, `chart`.
+
+Example (`src/locales/en/ftbotB.json`):
+
+```json
+{
+  "tradeList": {
+    "title": "Trades",
+    "columns": { "pair": "Pair", "profit": "Profit %" },
+    "alerts": { "tradeDeleted": "Trade {tradeId} deleted." }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+→ `t('ftbotB.tradeList.columns.profit')`. Generic example from the task brief:
+`trades.tradeList.columns.profit` = group `trades`, component `tradeList`, section `columns`.
+
+## 4. Using `t()`
+
+### 4.1 `<script setup>` + `<template>` (components, pages)
+
+```vue
+<script setup lang="ts">
+import { useI18n } from 'vue-i18n';
+
+const { t } = useI18n();
+
+// Labels that live in script must be computed, so they follow language changes:
+const options = computed(() => [
+  { value: 'left', label: t('settings.settingsPage.chart.scaleSideLeft') },
+  { value: 'right', label: t('settings.settingsPage.chart.scaleSideRight') },
+]);
+</script>
+
+<template>
+  <h3>{{ t('ftbotB.tradeList.title') }}</h3>
+  <!-- static attribute becomes a bound attribute -->
+  <UButton :label="t('common.actions.save')" :title="t('ftbotB.tradeList.hints.save')" />
+  <!-- interpolation -->
+  <span>{{ t('layout.navBar.version', { version: settingsStore.uiVersion }) }}</span>
+</template>
+```
+
+- Always use explicit `import { useI18n } from 'vue-i18n'` (it is not auto-imported).
+- `title="Foo"` → `:title="t('...')"`, `label="Foo"` → `:label="t('...')"`.
+- Template literals: `` :title="`Actions for ${trade.pair}`" `` →
+  `:title="t('ftbotB.tradeActionsPopover.title', { pair: trade.pair })"` with
+  `"Actions for {pair}"` / `"{pair} 操作"`.
+- `$t('...')` also works in templates (global injection), but prefer `t` from `useI18n()`.
+- If a component already has a variable named `t` (e.g. `v-for="t in tasks"` in
+  `BackgroundJobTracking.vue`), rename that variable.
+- `withDefaults` English default strings: keep the prop default empty and fall back at usage:
+  `{{ props.title || t('general.confirmDialogBox.defaultTitle') }}`.
+
+### 4.2 Plain TypeScript (stores, utils, composables)
+
+```ts
+import { t } from '@/i18n';
+
+export function deleteLock(lockId: number) {
+  // ...
+  showAlert(t('general.ftbotStore.alerts.lockDeleted', { lockId }), 'success');
+}
+```
+
+- Call `t()` **inside** functions / computed / getters - never at module top level
+  (a top-level `const LABEL = t('...')` is evaluated once, in the default language).
+- Module-level label arrays/objects (e.g. `availableBacktestMetrics` in `utils/backtestMetrics.ts`)
+  must become a `computed(...)` or a function. Keep their exported name and shape
+  (`{ field, header }`), because other files (`settings.vue`, `BacktestResultTablePer.vue`) use them.
+- Do not use translated text as an object key, id, sort key or comparison value. Keep a stable
+  internal key and translate only for display.
+
+### 4.3 ECharts option builders
+
+Option builders are usually `computed(() => ({ ... }))` - call `t()` inside, so the chart updates
+when the language changes:
+
+```ts
+const { t } = useI18n(); // in components; use `import { t } from '@/i18n'` in utils
+
+const chartOptions = computed((): EChartsOption => {
+  const profitLabel = t('chartsPages.hourlyChart.profitPercent');
+  const countLabel = t('chartsPages.hourlyChart.tradeCount');
+  return {
+    title: { text: t('chartsPages.hourlyChart.title') },
+    legend: { data: [profitLabel, countLabel] },
+    yAxis: [{ name: profitLabel }, { name: countLabel }],
+    series: [
+      { type: 'bar', name: profitLabel },
+      { type: 'line', name: countLabel },
+    ],
+  };
+});
+```
+
+- Module-level constants like `const CHART_PROFIT = 'Profit %'` move **inside** the computed.
+- `legend.data` and `series[].name` must use the same translated string (legend matches by name).
+- Where code matches series by name (e.g. `title === 'Volume'` in `useCandleChartTooltip.ts`,
+  `name: 'Stoploss'` in `tradeChartData.ts`) use a stable `id` for matching or compare against the
+  same `t()` result - don't break the matching.
+- Tooltip `formatter` functions run later; calling `t()` inside them is fine.
+- Indicator / column names coming from the strategy dataframe are data - don't translate them.
+
+### 4.4 Interpolation and pluralization
+
+```json
+// en
+"tradesSelected": "{count} trades selected",
+"openTrades": "no open trades | {n} open trade | {n} open trades"
+// zh-CN
+"tradesSelected": "已选择 {count} 笔交易",
+"openTrades": "无持仓 | {n} 笔持仓 | {n} 笔持仓"
+```
+
+```ts
+t('ftbotB.tradeList.tradesSelected', { count: 3 });
+t('ftbotB.tradeList.openTrades', trades.length); // n / count are passed implicitly
+```
+
+- Named placeholders only (`{pair}`), no positional `{0}`. Placeholder names must be identical
+  in en and zh-CN (the unit test checks this).
+- Chinese has no plural forms; a single form is fine (`"{n} 笔持仓"`), multiple forms are allowed.
+- Special characters in messages: `@` (linked message), `{`, `}` and `|` (plural separator)
+  must be written as literals: `{'@'}`, `{'{'}`, `{'}'}`, `{'|'}`.
+- No HTML in messages. For icons/links inside a sentence use the `I18nT` component with slots
+  (see `src/pages/settings.vue`):
+
+```vue
+<I18nT keypath="settings.settingsPage.ui.confirmDialogHintIcons" tag="span" scope="global">
+  <template #icons><i-mdi-alert class="inline" /></template>
+</I18nT>
+```
+
+### 4.5 Durations, dates, numbers
+
+- Durations: `humanizeDurationFromSeconds()` is already localized. Direct `humanizeDuration()`
+  calls must spread `getHumanizeDurationOptions()` from `@/i18n`.
+- Python timedelta strings from the bot (`avg_duration`, `drawdown_duration`, e.g.
+  `1 day, 2:00:00`): wrap them in `formatTimedelta()` (display only).
+- Dates: keep the numeric formatters in `utils/formatters/timeformat.ts`.
+- Numbers / percentages / prices: unchanged (formatters stay locale-neutral).
+
+## 5. What NOT to translate
+
+API field names, pair symbols (`BTC/USDT:USDT`), strategy names, enum values sent to the API,
+CSS classes, route paths, `console.log` / thrown developer errors, log lines coming from the bot,
+numbers, timeframes (`5m`), currency codes, exchange names, indicator/column names, and exit
+reasons / entry tags coming from the bot (`roi`, `stop_loss`, `exit_signal`, `force_exit` ... stay
+as sent). Keep `N/A` as-is (formatters and tests use it).
+
+Simple, fixed values from the bot may get a display mapping (trading / margin mode, order type,
+order side, `stake_amount: "unlimited"`, the dry-run balance note). Use a dynamic key with the
+raw value as fallback. `te(key)` without a locale argument checks the current and the fallback
+locale (vue-i18n 11.4+, pinned by a unit test), so a key missing in zh-CN still shows English:
+
+```ts
+const { t, te } = useI18n(); // or import { t, te } from '@/i18n' in plain TypeScript
+const key = `ftbotB.tradeList.orderTypes.${orderType}`;
+const label = te(key) ? t(key) : orderType; // display only, never sent back to the API
+```
+
+## 6. Checks before you hand in
+
+```bash
+pnpm build                    # also (re)generates src/auto-imports.d.ts, components.d.ts, typed-router.d.ts
+pnpm typecheck                # needs the generated *.d.ts from the build/dev server
+pnpm lint-ci
+pnpm test:unit --run          # includes tests/unit/i18n.spec.ts (key parity, placeholders, unknown keys)
+pnpm check-i18n               # scripts/check-i18n.mjs, see below
+pnpm test:e2e-chromium        # upstream Playwright tests, pinned to English (see below)
+```
+
+`scripts/check-i18n.mjs` (plain node, no build needed) fails on: locale JSON that does not parse,
+different group files or keys between `en` and `zh-CN`, empty messages, placeholder mismatch,
+unescaped `@ { } |`, keys used in `src/` that do not exist, and keys that are never used
+(the shared vocabulary in `common.json` is exempt and only counted). Keys built at runtime must
+keep a literal prefix (`` t(`ftbotB.tradeList.orderTypes.${type}`) ``) so the unused-key check
+can see them. It also prints warnings for likely-English text left in `.vue` templates (text
+nodes, `label=` / `title=` / `placeholder=` ... and string literals in bound UI attributes),
+for English literals in script code (`label:`, `title:`, `showAlert(...)`) and for hard-coded
+Chinese outside `src/locales`. Mark an intentional English script literal with a
+`// i18n-ignore: <reason>` comment on the same line, or extend `ALLOWED_TEXT` in the script.
+`--strict` turns warnings into a failure; `--root <dir>` checks another checkout.
+
+E2E: the upstream tests assert English texts, so `playwright.config.ts` pre-seeds the persisted
+settings (`ftUISettings.locale`) with `en`. `E2E_LOCALE=zh-CN pnpm test:e2e-chromium` runs them in
+Chinese (the text assertions then fail, which shows where upstream tests look at UI text).
+
+Screenshots: `pnpm build && node scripts/zh-screenshots.mjs --out <dir> [--locale en]` starts
+`vite preview`, mocks the whole bot API (e2e fixtures plus synthetic USDT-M futures trades) and
+the Iconify icon API, and saves 1440x900 screenshots of login, dashboard, trade, backtest
+(loaded result), chart and settings. Use it after every upstream upgrade to look for untranslated
+text and layout breakage.
+
+Note: on a fresh clone `pnpm typecheck` fails with ~1100 "Cannot find name" errors until a
+`vite build`, `vite` (dev) or `vitest` run has generated `src/auto-imports.d.ts`,
+`src/components.d.ts` and `src/typed-router.d.ts` (all gitignored). That is upstream behaviour,
+not an i18n problem - run `pnpm test:unit --run` or `pnpm build` before `pnpm typecheck`.
+
+Vitest's persistent module cache is disabled (`test.fsModuleCache: false` in `vite.config.ts`),
+otherwise newly added `src/locales/*/<group>.json` files would be invisible to `vitest` runs
+(stale `import.meta.glob` result) and the i18n spec would report their keys as missing.
+
+Then switch the language in Settings (中文 / English) and look at your screens in both languages.
+
+## 7. Upgrading upstream
+
+The localization is a patch series on top of the upstream tag:
+
+```bash
+git fetch --tags upstream
+git format-patch 3.2.1..zh-cn -o ../frequi-zh-patches   # export
+git checkout -b zh-cn-<new> <new-tag> && git am ../frequi-zh-patches/*.patch   # re-apply
+# or: git rebase --onto <new-tag> 3.2.1 zh-cn
+```
+
+After re-applying, run the checks above - `tests/unit/i18n.spec.ts` and `pnpm check-i18n`
+report keys that are used but missing or no longer used, and the `check-i18n` warnings list new
+English literals in changed upstream files that still need translating.
+
